{#-
  One page per GROUP rather than per case, because the four cases in a
  group answer one reader's question from four angles and a page each
  would be four pages of preamble. Every case keeps its own transcript,
  what it reads, and what setting it up takes.

  The transcript is the site's signature element and its whole job is to
  be concrete: a real question, a real answer, and a citation under the
  answer saying what was read to produce it. Nothing here is a promise
  about a feature that does not exist — every tool named is in
  /tools.json today.
-#}
<div class="page-head">
  <div>
    <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 6px">{{ group.group }}</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin: 0; max-width: 62ch">
      What people actually ask their agent, and what it reads to answer.
      The numbers in these exchanges are illustrative; the tools are real.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<nav class="sitelinks" style="justify-content: flex-start; padding: 0; margin: 18px 0 0; border: 0">
  {%- for g in usecases %}
  <a href="/use-cases/{{ g.cases[0].key }}"{% if g.group == group.group %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ g.group }}</a>
  {%- endfor %}
</nav>

{%- for c in group.cases %}
<section id="{{ c.key }}" style="margin-top: 34px; padding-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line)">
  <h2 class="page-title" style="font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 8px">{{ c.title }}</h2>
  <p class="lede" style="margin: 0 0 20px; max-width: 62ch; font-size: 16px">{{ c.lede | safe }}</p>

  {%- if c.script %}
  <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom: 18px">
    <div class="panel__head">
      <span>Tower Sage</span>
      <span class="footnote" style="font-weight: 400">your agent</span>
      <span class="mono" style="margin-left: auto; color: var(--ink-faint)">{{ c.script.tool }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
      {%- for line in c.script.lines %}
      {%- if line.role == "user" %}
      <p style="margin: 0; align-self: flex-end; max-width: 46ch; background: var(--panel-raised); border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 14px 14px 4px 14px; padding: 10px 14px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink)">{{ line.text | safe }}</p>
      {%- else %}
      <div style="align-self: flex-start; max-width: 62ch">
        <p style="margin: 0; background: var(--ground-sunken); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px 14px 14px 4px; padding: 11px 15px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-body); text-wrap: pretty">{{ line.text | safe }}</p>
        {%- if line.cite %}
        {#- The citation is the honest half: an answer with no sample
            behind it is an opinion. -#}
        <span class="footnote" style="display: inline-block; margin-top: 7px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; padding: 3px 10px">{{ line.cite | safe }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- endif %}

  <div style="display: flex; gap: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap">
    <section class="panel" style="flex: 1 1 320px">
      <div class="panel__head">What it reads</div>
      <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
        {%- for r in c.reads %}
        <span style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-body)">
          <span style="width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--accent-bright); flex: 0 0 auto; margin-top: 6px"></span>{{ r | safe }}
        </span>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="panel" style="flex: 1 1 240px">
      <div class="panel__head">To set this up</div>
      <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
        {%- for step in c.setup %}
        <span style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-body)">
          <span class="mono" style="color: var(--ink-faint)">{{ loop.index }}</span>{{ step | safe }}
        </span>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="panel__foot"><a href="/docs/quickstart">Quickstart ›</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endfor %}

<p class="footnote" style="margin: 28px 0 0; max-width: 78ch">
  Every tool named above is in <a href="/tools.json">the registry</a> and
  documented in <a href="/docs/tools">the tool reference</a>. What your agent
  can answer about YOU depends on what you track;
  <a href="/docs/recording">how recording works</a> explains the difference.
</p>
